{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Then you shall delight.</b> If you call the Sabbath day a delight, then you shall delight on YHWH, like a son who delights on the father, and I will make you ride on the heights of the earth — the heights of the earth, and it is the land of Israel." "<b>And I will feed you the heritage of Jacob.</b> The sense: behold, he speaks to the people of the exile, therefore 'and I will make you ride,' also 'who restores paths.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:11.510760421Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}